WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.700
Take it away,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.816
Hey everyone.

00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:12.800
I'm Dane.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.066
I'm a 3D art person
at Grinding Gear Games

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.366
I do a little bit more than that.

00:00:20.366 --> 00:00:22.250
I got my fingers
in a few different pies.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.466
I kind of know a bit about rigging
and animation.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.100
Come from a graphic design
background.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.333
So I'm a bit particular
about the 2D part of the item art.

00:00:33.416 --> 00:00:37.083
Despite being a 3D guy.

00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:39.300
So I'm going to get into the

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.050
the art aspect of Path of Exile 2’s items
and I'm going to pass over

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:43.916
to Hrishi afterwards.

00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:50.433
To talk about the the wonderful
numbers stuff you guys love so much.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.100
All right. So

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.950
Art in our game is,

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:59.150
you know, for items
is in two different sort of fields

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.366
of what we refer to as the 3D art,
which is what you see on the character.

00:01:02.366 --> 00:01:06.116
Obviously. And the 2D art, which is

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.300
I think
is actually the most important part.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.000
And I say this as the guy that spends
a lot of time modeling this stuff,

00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:15.166
the 2D art, is the part
that you're picturing in your

00:01:15.316 --> 00:01:18.266
in your head it’s the part that-

00:01:18.266 --> 00:01:21.266
it's the icons, iconic you know

00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:25.600
all the way back to the nineties like
when I was a kid playing Diablo 1

00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:28.583
you didn't see it on your character

00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:30.683
The inventory was
where you saw it.

00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:31.950
So it was the most important thing.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.183
So you look at this little icon
of like Griswold's Edge

00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:38.366
or the Butcher’s clever,
and you’d be like, Oh, that's so cool.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.766
That's fire damage.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:45.150
But For Path of Exile-

00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:49.766
For Path of Exile 1, obviously
you see your 2D art on your 3D model,

00:01:49.766 --> 00:01:51.416
but even to this day,

00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:54.416
there are still some uniques
that don't have any 3D art,

00:01:54.466 --> 00:01:57.450
which is a bit of a fail.

00:01:57.533 --> 00:01:59.633
That's not going to happen anymore.

00:01:59.633 --> 00:02:01.200
In Path of Exile 2 the 2D art

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.200
always comes from the 3D art

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.050
because we render it out
at high quality.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.116
In the past,

00:02:08.116 --> 00:02:10.550
the 2D art is a bit of a mishmash

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:13.550
of all sorts of stuff.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.016
This is random stuff
that I've grabbed

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.366
from the icons folder.

00:02:19.366 --> 00:02:22.366
Some of it looks like 3D models,
like a-posed,

00:02:22.366 --> 00:02:25.366
some of it's like a photo,
just a straight up photo.

00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:29.166
Some of it's like super cartoony,
like this guy down here.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.450
It it ends up
with a very inconsistent

00:02:33.533 --> 00:02:35.450
kind of front end to the game.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.133
Like, you guys are used to it.

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:38.633
You play the game so many years

00:02:38.633 --> 00:02:42.400
and items get added over time,
that it doesn't really matter.

00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:46.216
But it was always a bit of a problem
to me that things look inconsistent

00:02:46.216 --> 00:02:49.900
because different artists
have different approaches to how they

00:02:49.983 --> 00:02:52.700
just paint and render and do things
and sometimes they'll be like,

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.150
we need a unique yesterday.
So someone would just

00:02:57.233 --> 00:02:58.216
just get a photo of a

00:02:58.216 --> 00:03:02.100
shield, I guess

00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:05.183
so Path of Exile 2-

00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:09.000
these aren't the same items as the
previous screen, so don't freak out.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.150
That Kaom’s Heart now
looks like that

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:14.200
because that's not it.

00:03:14.266 --> 00:03:17.850
This is just an example
of similar sized stuff.

00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:21.500
Basically every single item,
even if it's a small thing,

00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:24.533
gets through the full treatment.

00:03:24.616 --> 00:03:26.600
I was modeling little gum nuts
for that

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.116
little potion bottle right there
just to render it.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:35.133
the flasks are all redone in 3D,
Everything's redone in 3D.

00:03:35.216 --> 00:03:39.483
And the goal is that you get
a consistent image on all the items.

00:03:39.566 --> 00:03:42.566
So everything in your inventory,
everything in your stash,

00:03:42.766 --> 00:03:45.716
it's going to look clean
and like it came from the same place

00:03:45.716 --> 00:03:49.300
because the rendering
is like the great equaliser.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:54.300
It doesn't paint a certain
way on this side or whatever.

00:03:54.383 --> 00:03:56.216
So everything's going to be clean.

00:03:56.216 --> 00:03:59.066
So this is an example of some shields

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.400
top is dex, bottom is
strength-dex

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.550
and we call
those obviously bucklers.

00:04:05.633 --> 00:04:09.200
And these ones we're calling a targe,
or I just call them a shield

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.150
because they're kind of
like the standard shield.

00:04:13.216 --> 00:04:16.216
These things
always highlighted a problem with me

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.750
in the game
because I'm a visual person

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.966
and I'd glance at stuff and I’d go,
What is that?

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.216
It's round and it's a shield.

00:04:23.216 --> 00:04:26.916
And I'd be like-
I'd have to like think a bit

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.266
For people that play the game
all the time,

00:04:29.266 --> 00:04:31.050
You get that vocabulary.
You know what it is

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.816
You've played it a million times,
you've seen all these items.

00:04:32.816 --> 00:04:36.666
But I think for a brand new game,
it's even more important to really

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.333
get things nice and clear. So

00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:42.650
what I'm doing with
all the main primary stat shields

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:47.500
is they all point that way
and the split ones go that way

00:04:47.566 --> 00:04:49.283
for stuff like this
where they're all round.

00:04:49.283 --> 00:04:53.116
I think it's really important
because again, as soon as it drops

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.266
a, the name, it's always going to be
something Buckler or a Targe

00:04:57.266 --> 00:05:00.266
and you just know, okay,
that's the thing thats dex.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.816
and it's
sitting in your inventory.

00:05:02.816 --> 00:05:05.150
You just-
you don't even have to -

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.150
You just glance at it and you’ll just - 
you’ll just know.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.116
Same thing with like
axes is a good example

00:05:11.116 --> 00:05:14.816
because axes to me always look
like they can be two handed

00:05:14.966 --> 00:05:18.600
or one handed, and they're kind of
frustrating to look at it again.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.233
I've chosen to make the one handed
go this way, two handed that way

00:05:22.316 --> 00:05:24.050
it's like a small thing

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.050
trying it out
and might get rolled back later.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.450
They might wind up
facing the same way.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.000
I personally like it

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.150
just a few base types from the acts.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.816
This isn't-

00:05:35.816 --> 00:05:37.166
This isn't by any means all of them.

00:05:37.166 --> 00:05:40.566
This is just some of them

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.483
like I said,

00:05:41.483 --> 00:05:44.366
even the small stuff
gets the same treatment.

00:05:44.366 --> 00:05:47.266
So we've got some amulets
and these three,

00:05:47.266 --> 00:05:49.250
I'll let you figure out
what they might do.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.800
But, yeah!

00:05:52.816 --> 00:05:54.150
They go through the same treatment.

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.000
We have a lot of control
because they're 3D rendered.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.450
We can try to just play around
with what they are- it's very hard

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.450
to get an artist to say, Hey,
I think I want this sword

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.050
this way and painted like that.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.000
And they go, well, I just have to
repaint the whole thing.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.883
Then I guess- which they don't.

00:06:11.966 --> 00:06:15.300
Currency orbs, same thing.

00:06:15.383 --> 00:06:18.233
And these were a fun one
because we got to redesign

00:06:18.233 --> 00:06:21.233
what we thought of them as

00:06:21.416 --> 00:06:23.483
previous head honcho

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:26.950
Erik, who's now retired.

00:06:27.016 --> 00:06:29.966
This was his little baby.

00:06:29.966 --> 00:06:35.350
He's actually printed massive scale,
cast bronze of these things.

00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:39.150
He's got a huge exalted orb
that's like this big.

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:42.866
But yeah, it was mostly
just to get them to be more cohesive.

00:06:42.866 --> 00:06:46.750
So they've got that same kind of-
That Roman

00:06:46.816 --> 00:06:51.750
kind of bust
head thing going on with a lot of them.

00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:52.250
Yeah.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.066
And so they all,

00:06:53.066 --> 00:06:57.783
they all get the same treatment,
even if they're a little guy,

00:06:57.866 --> 00:06:58.950
Some armours.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:04.950
So these are the base types for six
of the different

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:06.566
character branches.

00:07:06.566 --> 00:07:09.566
So, I don't know
if you're able to tell,

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.350
but there is a gradient
that occurs here.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:15.350
So it goes from dex, dex-int

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:19.950
int, int-strength,
strength, strength-dex

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:22.950
and it kind of
loops around where

00:07:23.066 --> 00:07:28.016
strength dex
looks a little lighter and it kind of-

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:31.100
that's a personal thing as well,
just trying to get things

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:35.600
to be very clearly gradients
across the items so that it feels

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.350
like you can just glance at stuff
and just know what it is.

00:07:40.433 --> 00:07:44.733
And this comes into
the naming of things, which is also,

00:07:44.816 --> 00:07:47.650
you know, as a visual person, it's
another thing.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:51.566
It actually had an impact on the art
in a cool way as well.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.116
So every single dex base type armour

00:07:54.116 --> 00:07:57.900
will be something vest
or something coat

00:07:57.983 --> 00:07:59.183
Same with all these

00:07:59.183 --> 00:08:01.200
They're all going to be called that

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.916
and you might go,
Oh, that's kind of limiting.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.616
But that limitation actually
kind of breeds

00:08:06.616 --> 00:08:11.516
really interesting creativity
to actually accentuate them more.

00:08:11.516 --> 00:08:14.850
And like I said,
you get a cool gradient that happens

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:19.950
as you go from- through the stats
and it loops back around.

00:08:20.033 --> 00:08:20.366
Yeah.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:25.916
So everything strength
will just look massive

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.650
like what’s the unique?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:32.800
The bronze one with the massive-

00:08:32.866 --> 00:08:35.783
Brass Dome?
Brass Dome! There's a base type that just

00:08:35.783 --> 00:08:39.716
is that big,
you know what I mean? Like-

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.766
Same thing with all the items.

00:08:42.766 --> 00:08:45.766
The pet peeve is when you're
working on all these things,

00:08:45.833 --> 00:08:48.650
so many things get called
boots, helmet,

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.816
gauntlets and after a while it just-
from the art managing side.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.300
I got really annoyed.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.300
I was just like, What is this again?

00:08:56.416 --> 00:08:59.150
And so it was like affecting
the management part

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:02.216
as well as me just reading stuff
in the game as well.

00:09:02.216 --> 00:09:05.966
So they're all going to be
basically partitioned

00:09:05.966 --> 00:09:09.266
in a way, naming wise
that affects the art a little bit.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:12.100
It's not
as strict as you would think.

00:09:12.166 --> 00:09:13.016
Like, say,

00:09:13.016 --> 00:09:16.016
if I go- I'll let you look at that
for a little bit.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.450
Like say there’s the gauntlets right?

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.766
They've got like- These ones here

00:09:19.766 --> 00:09:21.900
have got a bit of a leather bracer aspect

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.166
that kind of starts transitioning
over to what the dex ones do,

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:28.683
which will only focus
more on this area

00:09:28.766 --> 00:09:29.933
and they kind of spread out.

00:09:29.933 --> 00:09:33.933
And so there's more- more-

00:09:34.016 --> 00:09:36.683
Just more identity between them

00:09:36.683 --> 00:09:39.766
every like- Here’s a good example
actually versus Path of Exile 1

00:09:39.766 --> 00:09:43.366
because I think the dex-int gloves
are called the mittens.

00:09:43.366 --> 00:09:45.316
Right?
Mhm. Yep.

00:09:45.316 --> 00:09:48.983
And that always bothered me
because a mitten style

00:09:48.983 --> 00:09:52.050
gauntlet is actually a thing
and it's a very strong strength-y,

00:09:52.166 --> 00:09:53.116
bulky looking thing.

00:09:53.116 --> 00:09:55.966
So all the strength gauntlets
are now called Mitts,

00:09:55.966 --> 00:09:58.733
all the strength-dex ones are
the ones that are called Gauntlets.

00:09:58.733 --> 00:10:02.700
So every strength-dex Gauntlet will have this,
real chunky vibe that

00:10:02.783 --> 00:10:03.950
just separates itself.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.683
You're not going to
feel like it

00:10:06.683 --> 00:10:09.966
could blend across
three different classes.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:15.550
So I think we just get more
variety of gear this way.

00:10:15.616 --> 00:10:18.616
I think helmets is
the best example of the gradient

00:10:18.616 --> 00:10:23.800
I keep talking about, where Dex
is where I've got hoods,

00:10:23.866 --> 00:10:27.383
but you'll notice that dex-int
there's a hood strength-dex

00:10:27.383 --> 00:10:28.583
There's a hood.

00:10:28.583 --> 00:10:31.866
But the defining feature of that
is that it's a helmet

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.216
The defining feature of
that one is that there's a

00:10:34.216 --> 00:10:36.333
little covid mask in there.

00:10:38.833 --> 00:10:40.950
Yeah.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.866
So I've talked about base
types for a bit.

00:10:42.866 --> 00:10:46.350
So, now I'm going to go over
the difference between base types

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:52.150
and uniques in Path of Exile 2 
from an art perspective.

00:10:52.216 --> 00:10:55.216
It's something
most people don't think about,

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:59.033
but we're trying to treat
the base type items with very clear,

00:10:59.033 --> 00:11:02.116
distinct lighting, but
it's still stylistic.

00:11:02.116 --> 00:11:05.716
It's not just this flat, like
I just throw it in the render and hit

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.516
render type thing, like we have placed lights,

00:11:07.516 --> 00:11:11.283
and we've tried to make it
look as cool as it can.

00:11:11.366 --> 00:11:14.000
It's very clear and subtle.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.250
There's a bit of warm lighting,
a little bit of cool.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.266
That's about it.

00:11:17.266 --> 00:11:19.133
And the uniques
don't really have any rules.

00:11:19.133 --> 00:11:20.100
We just,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.916
we just sort of
make them look as bold and colorful

00:11:22.916 --> 00:11:25.533
and interesting as possible.

00:11:25.616 --> 00:11:28.433
And the other thing is every base
type in Path of Exile 2,

00:11:28.433 --> 00:11:33.633
will have a unique associated
with it at launch.

00:11:33.716 --> 00:11:35.416
Every single one of them

00:11:35.416 --> 00:11:38.666
and every single base
type has unique art in and of itself.

00:11:38.666 --> 00:11:40.250
There's no base type that repeats.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:43.283
You will not get a shield later
that has the same name-

00:11:43.466 --> 00:11:44.866
has a different name and same art

00:11:44.866 --> 00:11:49.533
Every single act has entirely unique
art all the way through the game.

00:11:49.616 --> 00:11:54.083
So to me,
the unique having a bit of a bond

00:11:54.083 --> 00:11:58.150
with the base type that it comes from
is kind of important

00:11:58.216 --> 00:12:01.866
because otherwise it kind of ruins
the item identity of both.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.950
If you had like a unique sword
that was like a scimitar looking

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:08.183
curvy thing, but the base type
was just a straight blade.

00:12:08.183 --> 00:12:09.716
It's kind of like,

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.933
shouldn't that be with the base type

00:12:11.933 --> 00:12:15.633
that has a curvy blade?
This is like kind of common sense to me.

00:12:15.716 --> 00:12:18.750
So the shield in the middle
is a pretty good example.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:21.383
They're very similar structurally,

00:12:21.383 --> 00:12:24.816
but very different in terms
of what actually happens.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:28.816
This one being super Celtic
and really ancient bronze looking

00:12:28.816 --> 00:12:34.500
and will do something very cool
with the numbers I imagine.

00:12:34.566 --> 00:12:35.516
This little Shield.

00:12:35.516 --> 00:12:42.250
I like a lot, this little Buckler
with a spooky man trapped in there.

00:12:42.316 --> 00:12:45.316
This is an example of
of the lighting of these things.

00:12:45.533 --> 00:12:49.383
So this is actually a unique armor
that they don't know about.

00:12:49.466 --> 00:12:51.600
Doesn't do anything yet

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.350
that's lit
how we would do a base type.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:58.800
And then here I remove it all and I
try to give it some more character,

00:12:58.883 --> 00:13:04.383
make it look a little bit more moody
and a little bit more special.

00:13:04.566 --> 00:13:08.716
we do this for all the items we
hand place and we pose the meshes

00:13:08.716 --> 00:13:11.783
and we try and get a really iconic
little look to it.

00:13:11.783 --> 00:13:16.716
So that's the difference
between those two things.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.800
And here I might get Hrishi to sort of
pitch me back in

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:25.600
because this is going over the act
specific run down of gear.

00:13:25.666 --> 00:13:27.616
So in each act

00:13:27.616 --> 00:13:30.466
you find the gear
specifically for that act.

00:13:30.466 --> 00:13:34.716
So all the base types will look like
they're very Maraketh in Act two.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.800
And as soon as you get to act three,
they're going to look very vaal

00:13:37.816 --> 00:13:40.433
and you purchase them?
 Yep.

00:13:40.433 --> 00:13:42.016
Just from the vendors?

00:13:42.016 --> 00:13:42.233
Yeah.

00:13:42.233 --> 00:13:43.816
So the vendors of each act

00:13:43.816 --> 00:13:46.816
only sell gear
that comes from that particular act.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.450
They don't sell like

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:52.166
you don’t go to act two
and buy Act one gear. 

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.116
And you just get more distinct looks.

00:13:56.116 --> 00:14:00.716
I personally really wanted
that gigantic stone Aztec Shield

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.666
and people were worried
it was too big.

00:14:02.666 --> 00:14:06.516
And I said
it might not be big enough for me.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.600
I wanted it this thick- anyway.

00:14:09.833 --> 00:14:13.883
So this sort of getting into the art

00:14:13.883 --> 00:14:18.033
focus of items in terms of

00:14:18.116 --> 00:14:21.000
some tropes
that happen with fantasy art in games

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.950
quite a lot, that kind of bugged me.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:27.866
All that stuff is obviously AI crap.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.416
But I mean, you know, it looks cool.

00:14:30.416 --> 00:14:35.666
When I was 13, I would be like, Hell
yeah, it's got spikes all over it.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.783
But after a while you've seen these,

00:14:38.783 --> 00:14:42.050
they're in everything
so many games that have that

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:46.450
and just loads of it
and you can infinitely produce-

00:14:46.516 --> 00:14:50.683
I mean AI just did four of
them like in half a second.

00:14:50.766 --> 00:14:54.266
Where as this stuff is from our world

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.233
and it goes back centuries
and there's just a rich history

00:14:57.233 --> 00:15:02.283
and culture behind all this art
making and weapon smithing from like

00:15:02.366 --> 00:15:03.150
just different

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:06.816
metal making practices
in all these different countries.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.716
India and like old cultures
like the Scythians

00:15:10.733 --> 00:15:12.683
and the Mongols
and how it all blends in.

00:15:12.683 --> 00:15:17.583
And I think artists need to do more
to really learn from the past,

00:15:17.666 --> 00:15:21.783
to make more interesting
looking stuff.

00:15:21.866 --> 00:15:25.516
This is what I want Path of Exile 2’s items
to feel more like, more like these

00:15:25.516 --> 00:15:30.066
really rich, dense things that have
all this history behind them.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.816
We do a lot of investigation on the

00:15:32.816 --> 00:15:37.383
on the environment side with stuff
like early on there was talks of like

00:15:37.466 --> 00:15:40.800
how the Maraketh
would write musical notation

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:41.700
and how that would affect

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:44.700
the sculptures on the walls
and like the environment art

00:15:44.716 --> 00:15:49.016
and then trying to get that into like
the item designs and stuff as well.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.000
So a lot of thought

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:53.783
goes on there to get things
to have a real rich sense of culture.

00:15:53.783 --> 00:15:56.666
Because for a game
that's all about items,

00:15:56.666 --> 00:15:58.516
you don't want everything
to just look like a jagged, spiky

00:15:58.516 --> 00:16:03.566
sword every single time
or like cool, flaming blade of-

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.650
like there's a place for them.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:10.816
But having just like a spoon, it's
just a weird spoon.

00:16:10.816 --> 00:16:11.850
and that’s the unique

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:17.966
It's kind of cool to me
There will be a spoon.

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.550
What is it going to do?

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:23.200
You figure that?

00:16:23.266 --> 00:16:26.266
So this is-
this is the part I really like,

00:16:26.483 --> 00:16:30.450
I personally
make a lot of weapons and items

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:33.666
and stuff, But the cool thing is
I make all these unique items.

00:16:33.683 --> 00:16:35.000
This is a drop, by the way.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.266
This is nothing

00:16:36.266 --> 00:16:39.683
they- if I could have a screen
that went all around

00:16:39.683 --> 00:16:42.266
the whole building,
it still wouldn't get them all.

00:16:42.266 --> 00:16:45.550
They'd keep going there’s many

00:16:45.616 --> 00:16:48.583
anyway, They don't know about them,
Most of the time...

00:16:48.583 --> 00:16:51.850
I'm just making them
and then I sort of,

00:16:51.916 --> 00:16:53.366
I sort of give it to them.

00:16:53.366 --> 00:16:55.050
And to me it's
kind of like they've found it.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:58.050
They've actually found a unique
and they don't know what it does.

00:16:58.283 --> 00:17:00.316
Like it's actually unidentified

00:17:00.316 --> 00:17:03.350
and they have to be their own
little Deckard Cain and be like,

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:06.383
What the hell does this do?

00:17:06.466 --> 00:17:07.733
Which is really exciting to me.

00:17:07.733 --> 00:17:11.750
Like, I don't know, this little
weird wand up the top

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:14.750
that is basically a hand
holding a bell.

00:17:14.933 --> 00:17:15.900
I just wanted a hand.

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:18.900
You hold a hand that holds a bell.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:21.900
And so I just think, well,
there's cool stuff there.

00:17:21.916 --> 00:17:24.716
Does it like, reverberate
your spells?

00:17:24.716 --> 00:17:27.266
Does it bounce things back?

00:17:27.266 --> 00:17:28.250
I don't know.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:29.783
It does stuff.

00:17:29.783 --> 00:17:32.333
It'll be cool, I promise.

00:17:32.333 --> 00:17:39.333
But- I have bad hearing,
I didn’t hear that.

00:17:39.416 --> 00:17:40.850
Anyway-

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.100
That's just a little tease of stuff.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.450
I just wanted to show you that,

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:49.233
the items in Path of Exile 2
are going to be very rich and

00:17:49.316 --> 00:17:52.633
every unique
is going to have a lot of interest

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:56.916
and just flair and just feel like it
came from somewhere.

00:17:56.916 --> 00:17:59.933
And it wasn't just like
it looks cool.

00:17:59.966 --> 00:18:02.000
Like some of them are just
they look cool,

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.916
but a lot of them are going
to be really well thought out

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.016
From the art side...

00:18:07.016 --> 00:18:09.150
I don't know about the numbers.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:14.350
This is where I pass over
to this guy.

00:18:14.416 --> 00:18:20.766
And thank you.

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:24.650
Hey, so let's talk about item
mechanics then.

00:18:24.833 --> 00:18:26.400
So my name is Hrishi

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:29.400
I'm a game designer at Grinding
Gear Games.

00:18:29.516 --> 00:18:31.400
I mostly work on item stuff.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:33.166
I've been working on them
for a really long time,

00:18:33.166 --> 00:18:37.016
although of course I do
other stuff as well,

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:40.100
so it is no secret

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.100
that we that we think items
are very important to this game.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.966
Like we just spent,
you know, all this time

00:18:44.966 --> 00:18:46.850
talking about
just what they look like.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.833
And there's so much more to them,
right?

00:18:48.833 --> 00:18:50.900
Like, we want items to feel real.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:54.450
They're more than just
a collection of stats.

00:18:54.533 --> 00:18:57.533
And now that  Path of Exile 2, is a game
in itself.

00:18:57.683 --> 00:19:01.133
We have a chance to look at items
all the way- At it's

00:19:01.133 --> 00:19:02.066
very fundamentals

00:19:02.066 --> 00:19:06.316
and try to make some changes that
we couldn't make in an existing game

00:19:06.533 --> 00:19:10.250
because of the worry of how
you would port existing items over

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.850
to a new system.

00:19:12.916 --> 00:19:16.766
So I'd like to go over some of
these fundamental changes with you.

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:22.300
So this is the first problem
that we really wanted to tackle,

00:19:22.366 --> 00:19:24.800
in Path of Exile 1

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:27.000
different weapon classes
don't necessarily

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:30.433
feel that different
from each other, like

00:19:30.516 --> 00:19:33.450
just take an axe and take a sword.

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:35.366
There are some light
stat differences, you know,

00:19:35.366 --> 00:19:36.500
some of them have,

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:40.450
you know, faster swing
speeds or faster damage per hit.

00:19:40.516 --> 00:19:44.800
But how- Like how much does
that difference actually matter?

00:19:44.866 --> 00:19:48.316
So for this reason,
we added implicits to all the weapons.

00:19:48.316 --> 00:19:52.250
So, you know, every sword
has an accuracy related implicit,

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:56.550
In most cases. Axes don't have
implicits, Maces have stun related.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.216
Implicits, and so on.

00:19:58.216 --> 00:19:59.416
And it helps.

00:19:59.416 --> 00:20:01.400
It gives them a bit of identity,

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:05.566
but it doesn't really make them feel
that different. Right?

00:20:05.566 --> 00:20:09.716
Like you'll still just swinging
a bunch of stats.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.833
The other problem too,
is that most skills you can use

00:20:12.833 --> 00:20:15.416
with kind of any weapons,
what you really care about

00:20:15.416 --> 00:20:17.700
is at the end of the day,
which is the weapon

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:22.900
that's going to do the most damage
and I'm going to use that weapon. So

00:20:22.966 --> 00:20:24.900
I want to talk about

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:28.166
the attribute
alignments in this game.

00:20:28.166 --> 00:20:32.750
And we consider this very important
as a way of aligning

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:37.900
certain attributes
with different mechanics in the game.

00:20:37.966 --> 00:20:39.300
There are some new weapons in there.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.300
I'll let you look to see
what they are.

00:20:42.316 --> 00:20:45.616
But effectively what we do is
we associate different weapons

00:20:45.766 --> 00:20:50.216
with different attributes
and that sort of gives us a

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:54.666
some guidance
on what their stats will be.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.500
For example, armor
related stats are usually aligned

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.950
to strength in our game, Evasion
is aligned to dexterity.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.933
Energy shield is aligned
 to intelligence

00:21:02.933 --> 00:21:05.666
and damage is no different, right?

00:21:05.666 --> 00:21:10.266
Strength aligned weapons
generally have higher

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:12.783
damage per individual hit.
Dex aligned

00:21:12.783 --> 00:21:16.383
weapons are usually faster
when it comes to their swing speeds

00:21:16.466 --> 00:21:17.150
and Int aligned

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:20.033
Weapons are usually really good
at dealing critical strikes.

00:21:20.033 --> 00:21:24.200
So, you know, using this as 
a baseline, it's

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.166
kind of clear that you know,

00:21:25.166 --> 00:21:28.166
a Mace is going to have higher damage
per individual hit,

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.833
whereas a Claw is going to be faster
and, you know, a

00:21:30.833 --> 00:21:34.416
Dagger is going
to have more crit and so on.

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.083
So we have tried to

00:21:36.083 --> 00:21:39.650
emphasise these differences
really heavily in Path of Exile 2

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:41.450
So I just have, you know,

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:44.150
a random dagger from the
from the dagger based types

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:45.350
picked up in a random axe.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:46.666
And you can see the difference
in critical

00:21:46.666 --> 00:21:50.466
strike chances is much higher
than what you might be used to.

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:53.216
So a dagger
is going to start with 15%

00:21:53.216 --> 00:21:55.466
and then you have mods
that improve it over and above that.

00:21:55.466 --> 00:21:56.850
So when you are using a dagger,

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:59.850
you're really going to feel like
you're like you're critting a lot.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.400
Whereas an axe,
you can see the, the base

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:05.250
damage of the weapon is going to be,
you know,

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:08.150
like per hit
is going to be quite a bit higher.

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:11.666
But all this
is going to change like how you view

00:22:11.666 --> 00:22:15.316
weapons, but it's still not
entirely enough as well,

00:22:15.566 --> 00:22:18.716
because ultimately the difference
between a mace and an axe,

00:22:18.716 --> 00:22:21.900
for example, is the sort of attacks
you can do with it.

00:22:21.983 --> 00:22:24.916
So in Path of Exile 2

00:22:24.916 --> 00:22:28.650
most attacks are going to be usable
with a single weapon.

00:22:28.733 --> 00:22:33.350
So this immediately makes designing
new attacks a lot more interesting

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:35.716
because you're not thinking
what's a cool attack?

00:22:35.716 --> 00:22:39.966
You're thinking what is a cool thing
that an axe in particular can do?

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:43.050
So let's talk about Axes.

00:22:43.166 --> 00:22:46.100
So Axes, as you can see from the

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:49.683
from the chart, they will be
slightly faster than maces.

00:22:49.683 --> 00:22:52.366
They do slightly less damage per
individual hit than a mace,

00:22:52.366 --> 00:22:54.316
but they're still primarily
strength aligned.

00:22:54.316 --> 00:22:57.000
So they're going to do
a lot of damage per hit.

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:59.150
But on top of this,
what defines an axe

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:03.933
thematically are themes
such as culling and executes.

00:23:04.016 --> 00:23:06.716
And in Path of Exile 2,
you can throw them.

00:23:06.716 --> 00:23:10.650
So that leads
to really interesting skill design

00:23:10.650 --> 00:23:12.716
because you can throw them,
wait for them to return.

00:23:12.716 --> 00:23:16.000
You know,
it's almost like a boomerang.

00:23:16.066 --> 00:23:18.533
Daggers. So daggers are

00:23:18.533 --> 00:23:21.716
sort of 50% in the Int section,
50% of the dex section.

00:23:21.716 --> 00:23:24.850
So they're both high crit

00:23:24.866 --> 00:23:28.450
and have decent swing speed,
but obviously per hit,

00:23:28.516 --> 00:23:31.466
their damage will be slow-
Will be lower.

00:23:31.466 --> 00:23:32.033
Thematically.

00:23:32.033 --> 00:23:33.916
What do you think of
when you think of a dagger?

00:23:33.916 --> 00:23:36.533
They're mostly
all about fast attacks,

00:23:36.533 --> 00:23:38.216
trying to find the weak
spot of enemies

00:23:38.216 --> 00:23:43.116
which sort of perfectly matches
what they are in this in this chart.

00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:44.966
And they're also
thematically linked to poison,

00:23:44.966 --> 00:23:48.633
which will really come out
in the skill design for daggers.

00:23:48.716 --> 00:23:52.083
So when you have this identity
of item class sorted in this way,

00:23:52.166 --> 00:23:54.116
you don't need to have an implicit

00:23:54.116 --> 00:23:56.300
that is on every single weapon
of that type.

00:23:56.300 --> 00:23:58.050
So we've removed them.

00:23:58.133 --> 00:24:01.650
All Swords do not have, you know,
an accuracy implicit,

00:24:01.733 --> 00:24:05.133
all daggers don't have, you know, a
crit implicit or whatever.

00:24:05.216 --> 00:24:07.616
So now that
the implicit slot is empty,

00:24:07.616 --> 00:24:10.966
we can make interesting implicits
that sort of make certain bases

00:24:10.966 --> 00:24:13.583
throughout the game
feel very different to each other

00:24:13.583 --> 00:24:15.416
because it's not really-

00:24:15.416 --> 00:24:17.416
it's not super interesting
if you're just going up

00:24:17.416 --> 00:24:20.333
a ladder of slightly stronger
and stronger bases.

00:24:20.333 --> 00:24:23.700
We want to throw something in there
to make the upgrades not feel too-

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:24.566
Too monotonous.

00:24:24.566 --> 00:24:26.816
So we've added some wacky implicits,

00:24:26.816 --> 00:24:30.150
and I'd like to show you
some of them.

00:24:30.233 --> 00:24:31.850
So this is an axe.

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:34.883
You'll find it at a certain level
and you might notice

00:24:34.883 --> 00:24:37.966
that this deals no Physical damage
what so ever.

00:24:37.966 --> 00:24:41.050
Its base Damage
is just pure fire.

00:24:41.116 --> 00:24:43.466
So this is going to give
you some interesting considerations

00:24:43.466 --> 00:24:45.350
when you find it, like
how are you going to build for it,

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:49.233
especially if the axe before
and the axe after is mostly physical.

00:24:49.316 --> 00:24:52.366
So it's not just that it's a damage
upgrade from the previous axe there-

00:24:52.466 --> 00:24:53.966
There are
there are these other interesting

00:24:53.966 --> 00:24:57.600
considerations
to think about as you go through.

00:24:57.683 --> 00:24:59.483
Here's another one.

00:24:59.483 --> 00:25:00.016
Yeah.

00:25:00.016 --> 00:25:01.350
So this is a mace

00:25:01.350 --> 00:25:04.350
that destroys enemies
that you kill with critical strikes.

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:07.016
Now, it's
it sounds pretty useful, right, that,

00:25:07.016 --> 00:25:10.016
you know, because who doesn't
want corpse removal on their weapon.

00:25:10.200 --> 00:25:11.900
But note that this is a mace.

00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:14.900
Maces are not necessarily that good
at dealing critical strikes.

00:25:15.150 --> 00:25:19.216
So it- So you know it
it could be useful

00:25:19.350 --> 00:25:20.366
but how do you make it

00:25:20.366 --> 00:25:23.366
useful it's not Int Aligned
so it's going to have low crit.

00:25:23.550 --> 00:25:26.516
There will be mods that can increase-
That can increase its crit.

00:25:26.516 --> 00:25:29.550
But still the way you build for it,
it's supposed to really make

00:25:29.550 --> 00:25:30.316
you think.

00:25:30.316 --> 00:25:33.166
It's not that it's
necessarily immediately useful.

00:25:33.166 --> 00:25:36.166
It's cool to have these sort of
thematic things throughout the game

00:25:36.383 --> 00:25:39.050
and it's just a puzzle piece
that is there, you know,

00:25:39.050 --> 00:25:42.050
so that sometime in the future
someone might find something

00:25:42.050 --> 00:25:46.800
that that they can do with this,
that only this would allow you to do.

00:25:46.883 --> 00:25:47.483
If some of you have

00:25:47.483 --> 00:25:50.483
played the demo
and have played the warrior class,

00:25:50.483 --> 00:25:54.483
you might have noticed that they have
a mechanic that breaks enemy armor.

00:25:54.566 --> 00:25:59.100
It's primarily a mace mechanic, but
there is a dagger that does it here.

00:25:59.166 --> 00:26:02.366
Like- the mace skills,
are normally the ones that interact

00:26:02.366 --> 00:26:05.116
with this in a number of ways.
But I mean a dagger does it.

00:26:05.116 --> 00:26:08.666
Breaking armor is obviously useful
and that makes this very special.

00:26:08.666 --> 00:26:09.800
And build defining.

00:26:09.800 --> 00:26:12.800
But how are you going to best
make use of something like this?

00:26:12.983 --> 00:26:15.983
Well, that's an exercise
left to the user.

00:26:15.983 --> 00:26:17.716
I'm sure there'll be a million
different

00:26:17.716 --> 00:26:21.550
broken things
that'll come out of all of this.

00:26:21.616 --> 00:26:24.833
So I've spent a bunch of time
talking about attack weapons.

00:26:24.833 --> 00:26:27.833
So let me briefly touch
on caster weapons.

00:26:27.866 --> 00:26:30.500
So in Path of Exile 1,
they were quite strange, right?

00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:33.333
Like you had a- like you had a staff

00:26:33.416 --> 00:26:34.216
and they had attack

00:26:34.216 --> 00:26:37.216
mod- They had attack attributes
and they could roll attack mods.

00:26:37.283 --> 00:26:39.083
But you're a mage,
you don't want to hit people

00:26:39.083 --> 00:26:41.033
with the staff,
you want to cast your spells.

00:26:41.033 --> 00:26:43.050
And as a result,
their mod pools are a lot worse

00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:46.050
because you have both attack
mods and spell caster mods rolling.

00:26:46.250 --> 00:26:48.166
Like of course they did improve
your spell caster mods,

00:26:48.166 --> 00:26:49.500
but because there were all these mods

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:52.500
rolling on the same item,
it was really hard to get a good one.

00:26:52.733 --> 00:26:54.866
We tried a bunch of band aid fixes
over the years.

00:26:54.866 --> 00:26:58.616
Like I'm sure you're well aware of us
introducing Rune daggers and

00:26:58.700 --> 00:27:01.583
splitting staves
into regular staves and war staves,

00:27:01.583 --> 00:27:04.433
but they didn't really fix
the underlying issue.

00:27:04.433 --> 00:27:08.666
So we feel it's better to break
out these concepts entirely

00:27:08.750 --> 00:27:11.850
so, in Path of Exile 2

00:27:11.850 --> 00:27:14.333
Wands And Staves will have no attack
stats whatsoever.

00:27:14.333 --> 00:27:18.750
They just come with a skill
that costs no mana.

00:27:18.833 --> 00:27:22.216
These spells can be a number
of things from just a straight up

00:27:22.216 --> 00:27:26.033
damage spell like this one,
which is the first staff you get as

00:27:26.033 --> 00:27:29.033
you wash up on the beach
or a number of other things

00:27:29.116 --> 00:27:33.400
that can be used alongside
your other skills.

00:27:33.466 --> 00:27:35.750
The later ones
obviously tend to have a few more

00:27:35.750 --> 00:27:37.466
interesting considerations.

00:27:37.466 --> 00:27:40.350
Like this one obviously
will be very familiar with anyone

00:27:40.350 --> 00:27:44.916
who's played Path of Exile where this lets
you triple cast your next skill,

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:50.133
which is obviously really good
for skills with really long cast times.

00:27:50.216 --> 00:27:57.633
Here's an example of-

00:27:57.716 --> 00:28:00.500
pretty fun, right?

00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:01.850
So you might be wondering

00:28:01.850 --> 00:28:05.066
what about people
that want to hit people with staves?

00:28:05.150 --> 00:28:07.816
So we have split out
the melee portion of staves

00:28:07.816 --> 00:28:10.100
into its own weapon
class called a quarterstaff.

00:28:10.100 --> 00:28:12.900
And it's sort of
thematically linked to the monk.

00:28:12.900 --> 00:28:14.850
But again, this is Path of Exile.

00:28:14.850 --> 00:28:17.850
Anyone can use any weapon
and do anything.

00:28:18.016 --> 00:28:20.850
All the mods here
are obviously attack related mods

00:28:20.850 --> 00:28:22.700
and here is a
particularly interesting one

00:28:22.700 --> 00:28:25.850
which has a longer range
than every other quarterstaff.

00:28:26.033 --> 00:28:28.916
And you can actually see its art
looking longer

00:28:28.916 --> 00:28:30.000
than the others in-game.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:34.300
If you compare the
two quarter staves together.

00:28:34.366 --> 00:28:37.050
So we've talked about the two,

00:28:37.050 --> 00:28:40.950
I would say core archetypes
that we sort of support in Path of

00:28:40.950 --> 00:28:43.200
Exile one,
with attackers and spell casters.

00:28:43.200 --> 00:28:48.083
But trappers and miners
of course, are another archetype

00:28:48.083 --> 00:28:49.750
that sort of got left in the dust
a little bit.

00:28:49.750 --> 00:28:51.800
In Path of Exile 1,
They were fully supported

00:28:51.800 --> 00:28:53.666
with a bunch of skills
and everything,

00:28:53.666 --> 00:28:57.116
but they didn't really have gear that
was specifically designed for them.

00:28:57.200 --> 00:29:00.266
They just sort of used,
you know, caster weapons because,

00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:03.700
you know, it increased
the damage of their skills.

00:29:03.766 --> 00:29:07.366
But it's really thematically weird
because they're not a mage.

00:29:07.366 --> 00:29:10.916
They're supposed to be mechanically
aligned and that sort of thing.

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:12.716
So we wanted to add

00:29:12.716 --> 00:29:16.000
an item type that can be used
specifically with trappers.

00:29:16.066 --> 00:29:19.250
So the first major change is traps
are no longer spells,

00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:22.800
traps are just trap damage
and there will be ways to improve.

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:26.816
Specifically trap damage
that are not related to spells.

00:29:26.900 --> 00:29:28.166
So, this is an

00:29:28.166 --> 00:29:31.466
example of the new base type
that you can use and your main hand,

00:29:31.550 --> 00:29:34.550
it takes both your hands
and you can see that

00:29:34.766 --> 00:29:38.800
the throw time of the trap is listed
on the item itself.

00:29:38.866 --> 00:29:43.650
And yes, that means you can modify
it further with mods on the item.

00:29:43.733 --> 00:29:46.583
The other thing you might notice
is that

00:29:46.583 --> 00:29:49.400
it has a detonation type.

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:51.500
That is because we have sort of

00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:54.650
combined the concept of trappers
and miners into one thing.

00:29:54.683 --> 00:29:58.083
Mines are also trap skills,
but with a different detonation type.

00:29:58.166 --> 00:30:02.216
So you can take any trap skill,
swap your weapon that you're using

00:30:02.216 --> 00:30:03.833
and it's now a mine.

00:30:03.833 --> 00:30:06.683
It's not that you have
to specifically find a mine skill

00:30:06.683 --> 00:30:10.000
to use, you know, to
to actually have that playstyle.

00:30:10.066 --> 00:30:12.950
And the other interesting thing
is with the new weapons

00:30:12.950 --> 00:30:16.316
swapping system, you can have a trap
in your alternate weapon set.

00:30:16.516 --> 00:30:19.733
So you can still use other skills,
but still trap occasionally

00:30:19.733 --> 00:30:22.833
if you really want to as well.

00:30:22.916 --> 00:30:24.833
I do have an example of a mine as well.

00:30:24.833 --> 00:30:26.250
So this one, as you can see,

00:30:26.250 --> 00:30:28.100
will have the detonation type,
which is manual,

00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:30.416
which requires you
to detonate them afterwards.

00:30:30.416 --> 00:30:33.633
And yes, just like all the weapons
there will be implicits

00:30:33.716 --> 00:30:36.350
on some of these
throughout the progression.

00:30:36.350 --> 00:30:42.033
So you'll have these interesting
considerations on trappers as well.

00:30:42.116 --> 00:30:46.050
So the other archetype
that doesn't- That never had,

00:30:46.133 --> 00:30:49.733
you know, a specific item class
dedicated to it was minion builds

00:30:49.733 --> 00:30:53.066
and you know, general support
type characters

00:30:53.150 --> 00:30:56.416
like we've tried a bunch of,
you know, band aid fixes over the years

00:30:56.416 --> 00:30:57.950
like,
you know, about the convoking wand

00:30:57.950 --> 00:30:58.433
and we've added

00:30:58.433 --> 00:31:00.166
bone rings
and we've done a few of those things,

00:31:00.166 --> 00:31:02.266
but they don't really fix
the root of the problem.

00:31:02.266 --> 00:31:03.200
They do help.

00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:05.300
But you know, what you really want

00:31:05.300 --> 00:31:07.733
is a set of items
that you can find throughout the game

00:31:07.733 --> 00:31:11.883
that is specifically for,
you know, this particular class.

00:31:11.966 --> 00:31:15.300
And we, as you know,
we've added spirit as a concept,

00:31:15.300 --> 00:31:19.050
which is for our skills that were
previously reserving your mana,

00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:22.966
but it also is about your like
permanent minions

00:31:22.966 --> 00:31:24.316
also use your spirit.

00:31:24.316 --> 00:31:25.800
So if you want more zombies,

00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:27.900
there's no such thing
as just getting plus zombies.

00:31:27.900 --> 00:31:30.150
It's just increasing
Your spirit gives you more zombies.

00:31:30.150 --> 00:31:32.450
You can use as much of
as much of your spirit as you like.

00:31:32.450 --> 00:31:34.166
To get as many zombies as you like.

00:31:34.166 --> 00:31:37.166
It is completely dependent on
how much spirit you have.

00:31:37.350 --> 00:31:40.050
So we obviously wanted a base type
to support this and scepters

00:31:40.050 --> 00:31:41.816
are thematically perfect
for this kind of thing

00:31:41.816 --> 00:31:43.200
because they were also kind of weird.

00:31:43.200 --> 00:31:47.016
with the whole half attack half
spell caster type of thing.

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:51.483
So I have some
examples of scepters here.

00:31:51.566 --> 00:31:52.950
As you can see,

00:31:52.950 --> 00:31:56.700
the mods almost always grant
aura like effects

00:31:56.783 --> 00:31:59.700
or they improve the spirit
on the item itself.

00:31:59.700 --> 00:32:01.350
So it's almost like you get to build

00:32:01.350 --> 00:32:05.100
your own aura and hold it in either
your main hand or your off-hand.

00:32:05.183 --> 00:32:07.400
You get to have that flexibility
where you know,

00:32:07.400 --> 00:32:10.350
if you're not planning on doing much
attacking or spell casting yourself,

00:32:10.350 --> 00:32:12.866
then hold it in your main hand,
have a shield

00:32:12.866 --> 00:32:15.233
and you're pretty defensive
and you get to buff your allies.

00:32:15.233 --> 00:32:18.233
or your minions- Well,
your allies and your minions,

00:32:18.233 --> 00:32:19.100
I should say.

00:32:19.100 --> 00:32:22.200
But if you want to, let's say,
do some attacking as well,

00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:24.316
then you can just hold it
in your off-hand if you like,

00:32:24.316 --> 00:32:26.250
and then you can still have a weapon
in your main hand.

00:32:26.250 --> 00:32:28.766
You can do some damage,
you know, for something like,

00:32:28.766 --> 00:32:30.300
you know, a build
that would be similar

00:32:30.300 --> 00:32:32.100
to dominating blow,
you can still have a weapon

00:32:32.100 --> 00:32:35.350
and you can still buff
your minions in your off-hand.

00:32:35.416 --> 00:32:37.283
You can also
put it in your alternate weapon set

00:32:37.283 --> 00:32:38.516
if you want to just

00:32:38.516 --> 00:32:41.450
buff your allies once in a while
and not all the time,

00:32:41.450 --> 00:32:43.733
but just be careful
not to use the extra spirit

00:32:43.733 --> 00:32:45.150
that you gain to use your minions,

00:32:45.150 --> 00:32:50.350
because when you swap out,
your minions will go away.

00:32:50.416 --> 00:32:53.250
So we've talked a bit about skills
before.

00:32:53.250 --> 00:32:56.516
So as
you might have seen in the keynote,

00:32:56.600 --> 00:33:01.366
we had a big problem with how skill
gems dropped in Path of Exile 1

00:33:01.366 --> 00:33:04.833
because the more skill gems
we add,

00:33:04.916 --> 00:33:08.066
the less chance you have of finding
the one that you particularly want.

00:33:08.300 --> 00:33:11.483
And because- To solve this problem,
we added gem vendors in

00:33:11.483 --> 00:33:12.350
Path of Exile 1

00:33:12.350 --> 00:33:14.566
So you could get one
at any time that you like.

00:33:14.566 --> 00:33:17.400
But that isn't 
the correct solution, because what

00:33:17.400 --> 00:33:20.400
that means is it's just trivial
to get any gem at any time.

00:33:20.550 --> 00:33:22.216
And at that point,
why are they even itemised?

00:33:22.216 --> 00:33:24.466
like you should just have access
to your skills? Right?

00:33:24.466 --> 00:33:27.083
So in Path of Exile 2,
we wanted to both

00:33:27.083 --> 00:33:30.366
have the fun moment where you find
a gem of like a higher tier.

00:33:30.450 --> 00:33:33.650
But also we wanted to not prevent you
from just using a skill

00:33:33.650 --> 00:33:37.500
that you want to use
at that particular time.

00:33:37.583 --> 00:33:38.116
So we've added

00:33:38.116 --> 00:33:41.116
Uncut Gems, so regular skill gems
no longer drop

00:33:41.366 --> 00:33:42.166
and you just find

00:33:42.166 --> 00:33:45.300
uncut gems of a certain tier
and you can use them

00:33:45.300 --> 00:33:48.300
to turn them into any skill
of that particular tier.

00:33:48.300 --> 00:33:49.966
And they come pre-leveled.

00:33:49.966 --> 00:33:52.550
So what that means is

00:33:52.550 --> 00:33:55.066
it's a lot easier
to switch into a new skill

00:33:55.066 --> 00:33:55.800
because you don't have to

00:33:55.800 --> 00:33:59.216
then re level that skill from level
one and wait for, you know,

00:33:59.300 --> 00:34:01.283
wait for the wait for the damage
to come back to

00:34:01.283 --> 00:34:03.600
what the current skill
it was that you were using.

00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:07.350
Like you can just seamlessly
swap from one to the other.

00:34:07.433 --> 00:34:10.433
What this means is certain
gems just don't exist at low levels.

00:34:10.616 --> 00:34:14.400
For example, I think Firestorm is
a 28 skill in Path of Exile 1

00:34:14.483 --> 00:34:18.683
So in this- So here you might find-
You might get

00:34:18.683 --> 00:34:25.750
firestorm at level five and levels
below level five just don't exist

00:34:25.816 --> 00:34:27.866
So this is- oh- So let's get

00:34:27.866 --> 00:34:31.150
into the meat of the matter
which is item drops.

00:34:31.216 --> 00:34:35.016
As you all know, we want item
drops on the ground to matter more.

00:34:35.100 --> 00:34:36.916
You generally don't
pick up rares on the ground

00:34:36.916 --> 00:34:38.750
because you know,
if you're going to pick them up

00:34:38.750 --> 00:34:40.666
nine times out of ten,
they're probably going to suck,

00:34:40.666 --> 00:34:41.916
right like that?

00:34:41.916 --> 00:34:43.766
Like you're not going to use them

00:34:43.766 --> 00:34:45.316
there are a number of reasons
for this,

00:34:45.316 --> 00:34:48.050
and we are trying to address
a lot of these reasons

00:34:48.050 --> 00:34:49.483
when we're when we're redoing
item drops

00:34:49.483 --> 00:34:51.900
from the ground up
and in Path of Exile 2

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:54.750
But there is one particular reason
that I wanted to talk about,

00:34:54.750 --> 00:34:59.050
and that is actually because
of how the chaos orb functions.

00:34:59.116 --> 00:35:03.566
So if I pick up,
let's say a helmet of item level 70

00:35:03.683 --> 00:35:07.266
and another helmet of item level 70,
and I use a chaos orb on both of them,

00:35:07.350 --> 00:35:09.716
it doesn't matter
what you pick them up-

00:35:09.716 --> 00:35:11.783
it doesn't matter what item
it was that you picked up originally

00:35:11.783 --> 00:35:13.700
because they're now completely
new items.

00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:15.616
The only thing that mattered
is the item

00:35:15.616 --> 00:35:17.366
level of the item that it started
with.

00:35:17.366 --> 00:35:18.650
In both cases,

00:35:18.650 --> 00:35:21.650
the mods that they came with
just no longer matter anymore.

00:35:21.866 --> 00:35:24.533
So every base type is effectively
the same, just as good

00:35:24.533 --> 00:35:25.550
as every other base type

00:35:25.550 --> 00:35:29.316
for the purposes of, you know, for
for the purposes of a Chaos Orb anyway

00:35:29.400 --> 00:35:33.550
So picking up a rare at that point
is identical to using a single Chaos Orb

00:35:33.616 --> 00:35:35.733
on that same base type.

00:35:35.816 --> 00:35:36.766
So we're

00:35:36.766 --> 00:35:40.683
making a change to how Chaos Orbs work
in Path of Exile 2.

00:35:40.766 --> 00:35:44.550
So rather than rerolling
the item entirely, it

00:35:44.633 --> 00:35:48.483
replaces one mod on the item,
just one.

00:35:48.566 --> 00:35:51.200
So this means the item that you start

00:35:51.200 --> 00:35:54.200
with matters a whole lot more
when it comes to this

00:35:54.383 --> 00:35:57.700
because you pick up a rare
it has, you know,

00:35:57.766 --> 00:36:01.166
two to three great mods,
maybe one or two really bad mods.

00:36:01.316 --> 00:36:03.383
Those rares previously
were not going to be useful

00:36:03.383 --> 00:36:05.783
because it didn't matter
that it had a few good mods

00:36:05.783 --> 00:36:08.783
because it also had those bad mods
that sort of made the item not worth-

00:36:09.016 --> 00:36:10.066
not worth using.

00:36:10.066 --> 00:36:12.616
But now what you can do
is you can just,

00:36:12.616 --> 00:36:15.500
you know, like every item
could be one or two chaos orbs away

00:36:15.500 --> 00:36:17.450
from becoming a really great item,

00:36:17.450 --> 00:36:19.766
whereas previously those
rares were still not good

00:36:19.766 --> 00:36:22.350
because they didn't
have those good mods and now you will-

00:36:22.350 --> 00:36:25.366
And now I- You will hopefully
use your chaos orbs

00:36:25.583 --> 00:36:28.366
for a lot of these sort of near
miss rares.

00:36:28.366 --> 00:36:29.216
Just use one.

00:36:29.216 --> 00:36:33.233
And if it- If it doesn't work out
well the item wasn't that- Wasn't

00:36:33.233 --> 00:36:37.116
that fantastic to begin with anyway
because it still had those bad mods.

00:36:37.183 --> 00:36:40.283
But if one of those bad mods
turns into a good one

00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:41.516
then that would be fantastic.

00:36:41.516 --> 00:36:45.566
and that would
really improve this.

00:36:45.650 --> 00:36:47.783
This feeling of the
items on the ground mattering more.

00:36:47.783 --> 00:36:51.183
Because what you started with
now is of paramount importance.

00:36:51.266 --> 00:36:54.300
But if this was the only change,
then the best way to make items

00:36:54.300 --> 00:36:57.300
would be to,
you know, start from a magic item.

00:36:57.466 --> 00:37:00.150
Spam your alterations.
How ever many thousands

00:37:00.150 --> 00:37:03.050
it would take, and then regal
and then do that.

00:37:03.050 --> 00:37:05.250
So for that reason
we are making a few changes.

00:37:05.250 --> 00:37:07.216
But the first one is that we

00:37:07.216 --> 00:37:11.516
alteration orbs will no longer exist
in Path of Exile 2

00:37:11.600 --> 00:37:14.900
So the way to do this is
you must start with a good magic item

00:37:14.900 --> 00:37:15.983
or a good rare item,

00:37:15.983 --> 00:37:18.233
or you can create
one with the transmute or a chaos orb.

00:37:18.233 --> 00:37:23.850
Now to help all these changes,
we have gone through every single

00:37:23.933 --> 00:37:27.333
item and looked at that mod pool
and made changes to every single

00:37:27.416 --> 00:37:28.366
items mod pool

00:37:28.366 --> 00:37:31.616
So almost everything will be
different to help you with this.

00:37:31.700 --> 00:37:36.450
With this process
of making item drops matter more.

00:37:36.533 --> 00:37:37.216
So to

00:37:37.216 --> 00:37:41.100
quickly wind up,
I want to touch on unique items.

00:37:41.183 --> 00:37:43.966
Oh. Oh, there we go.

00:37:43.966 --> 00:37:45.983
Our philosophy on unique
items is that

00:37:45.983 --> 00:37:48.983
they must be the best item
for somebody,

00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:53.016
but most uniques should not be
the best item for everybody.

00:37:53.100 --> 00:37:54.016
Now obvious-

00:37:54.016 --> 00:37:57.416
now we obviously feel like unique
items are very important to us.

00:37:57.416 --> 00:37:58.500
And as Dane mentioned,

00:37:58.500 --> 00:38:02.500
we want to have a unique item
on every single base type.

00:38:02.566 --> 00:38:06.050
Some of you may not know this,
but before I started working at GGG,

00:38:06.300 --> 00:38:10.700
I was- I designed one of the supporter
uniques way back in the day.

00:38:10.700 --> 00:38:11.483
So I have

00:38:11.483 --> 00:38:15.416
I have had- I have had massive love
for the unique items in this game.

00:38:15.566 --> 00:38:19.250
The supporter unique that I made
back in 2013 was Cloak of Defiance

00:38:19.500 --> 00:38:22.833
which resulted
in the Mind Over Matter Keystone.

00:38:22.916 --> 00:38:24.533
And I've
been involved in making unique

00:38:24.533 --> 00:38:28.400
items ever since breach
which is 2016.

00:38:28.400 --> 00:38:31.016
So it's been it's been quite a while.

00:38:31.016 --> 00:38:35.816
So we want to make many unique items
for everybody.

00:38:35.900 --> 00:38:38.000
They are meant to enable wacky
things.

00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:41.000
They are meant to let you do things
that you thought

00:38:41.150 --> 00:38:46.016
would never be possible
and possibly be build defining.

00:38:46.016 --> 00:38:49.366
So I have an example
of a low level unique that we made.

00:38:49.366 --> 00:38:53.166
I wish we had more to show you,
but this one here is

00:38:53.250 --> 00:38:56.216
is pretty interesting
in that it always freezes

00:38:56.216 --> 00:38:59.216
enemies for its full duration
when you hit them the first time.

00:38:59.216 --> 00:38:59.816
So you always

00:38:59.816 --> 00:39:03.566
have a really strong initiation
as soon as you walk up to an enemy.

00:39:03.650 --> 00:39:08.066
So like men- Like Dane mentioned,
every base type will have a unique

00:39:08.150 --> 00:39:10.816
and that and that includes
a lot of new uniques.

00:39:10.816 --> 00:39:12.533
But don't worry

00:39:12.533 --> 00:39:15.166
what this also means is
we are going to be bringing a lot

00:39:15.166 --> 00:39:18.816
of your favorites from Path of Exile 1
into Path of Exile 2

00:39:18.900 --> 00:39:21.800
because is it really-
Is it really a Path of Exile game

00:39:21.800 --> 00:39:25.616
if you don't have a
Headhunter or a Shavs in it?

00:39:25.700 --> 00:39:26.816
Yeah, exactly.

00:39:26.816 --> 00:39:30.250
So they might be slightly different
to what you might-

00:39:30.366 --> 00:39:31.166
You might be used to,

00:39:31.166 --> 00:39:32.716
you know,
a few stats might be different here

00:39:32.716 --> 00:39:34.800
and there as a result
of the mechanics changing,

00:39:34.800 --> 00:39:37.283
but they will be instantly
recognisable as a result.

00:39:37.283 --> 00:39:37.750
And you'll

00:39:37.750 --> 00:39:40.850
have a lot of your favorites
that you’re used to- That you-

00:39:40.966 --> 00:39:42.950
That you used to like playing
with in Path of Exile 1

00:39:42.950 --> 00:39:47.850
And you will have a lot of new ones
as well to find as you go through.

00:39:47.933 --> 00:39:52.800
So I think that's everything
from my end.

00:39:52.883 --> 00:39:56.166
I guess we have some time
for questions.

00:39:56.250 --> 00:40:02.966
Come on, Zaccie.

00:40:03.050 --> 00:40:03.450
Hello.

00:40:03.450 --> 00:40:06.533
My name's
Zac and I'm a game designer for GGG,

00:40:06.650 --> 00:40:08.716
and I will be doing the questions
here.

00:40:08.716 --> 00:40:11.933
And while I wait for people
to submit some questions,

00:40:11.933 --> 00:40:15.816
I will ask one I prepared earlier,
and that is

00:40:15.900 --> 00:40:19.400
does the art of the item
dictate the design

00:40:19.400 --> 00:40:23.050
or do you design first
and then get the art for the item?

00:40:23.116 --> 00:40:27.416
It can be very different depending on
what is necessary at the time.

00:40:27.500 --> 00:40:28.283
Like sometimes

00:40:28.283 --> 00:40:31.283
we just have to make a lot of uniques
in a really short amount-

00:40:31.433 --> 00:40:32.666
amount of time.

00:40:32.666 --> 00:40:36.100
And if we have art available,
then we try to fit the stat

00:40:36.166 --> 00:40:38.750
to what the unique art
is already there.

00:40:38.750 --> 00:40:41.666
But generally sometimes it's,
you know,

00:40:41.666 --> 00:40:45.450
we have this crazy idea
that we're like, Can we do this?

00:40:45.450 --> 00:40:47.716
And it's like, Well,
it sounds cool, let's do it.

00:40:47.716 --> 00:40:49.766
And we make an item
and it's just a blank item

00:40:49.766 --> 00:40:51.466
without a name, without any art.

00:40:51.466 --> 00:40:52.583
And then we try it and game.

00:40:52.583 --> 00:40:55.916
It's like this unique is awesome
and then we make the art for it

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:57.416
so it can go both ways.

00:40:57.416 --> 00:41:01.216
I would say more often than not,
at least in Path of Exile 1, it's

00:41:01.216 --> 00:41:06.100
been mechanics first into art,
but you know that may not be

00:41:06.166 --> 00:41:09.683
Yeah and for Path of Exile 2
It's more the opposite for now

00:41:09.683 --> 00:41:11.666
because for a long time

00:41:11.666 --> 00:41:14.966
they didn't really know
what they were doing with items

00:41:15.050 --> 00:41:19.333
and as basically a blacksmith that just
smashes things out really quickly.

00:41:19.383 --> 00:41:21.383
It's just like that's a cool sword

00:41:21.383 --> 00:41:25.500
that's a cool sword, that's a cool sword.
I just make all this stuff and

00:41:25.583 --> 00:41:26.400
yeah, they're going

00:41:26.400 --> 00:41:29.400
to find that treasure trove of stuff
and turn it into stuff.

00:41:29.400 --> 00:41:32.416
But I think it's really valuable
to have art

00:41:32.416 --> 00:41:35.450
that can inspire gameplay stuff
that they weren't even thinking of.

00:41:35.450 --> 00:41:38.716
They might not even have- Never
entered their mental space.

00:41:38.716 --> 00:41:40.550
Oh yeah, that happens a lot.
I would say.

00:41:40.550 --> 00:41:42.900
They'll just see it and go, Oh,
this thing's like split in two.

00:41:42.900 --> 00:41:46.666
And it could be like,
you know, it hits the guy here.

00:41:46.666 --> 00:41:48.150
I don't know

00:41:52.616 --> 00:41:54.833
So let's
see what else we've got here.

00:41:54.833 --> 00:41:57.600
Do you have any memorable uniques

00:41:57.600 --> 00:42:00.383
from Path of Exile 1
that you have designed?

00:42:00.383 --> 00:42:07.416
Oh, that is a tough question
because I've made so many,

00:42:07.500 --> 00:42:09.566
I think one of my favorites,

00:42:09.566 --> 00:42:12.866
or at least I would say
very memorable, was Indigon

00:42:12.950 --> 00:42:18.183
because Indigon was probably
the start of that entire set of

00:42:18.266 --> 00:42:21.016
mana related spells
that followed later.

00:42:21.016 --> 00:42:22.583
But Indigon
was really the first.

00:42:22.583 --> 00:42:27.050
It was the first item that weaponised
mana into a form of damage.

00:42:27.116 --> 00:42:29.416
I have a thing for that as well.

00:42:29.416 --> 00:42:29.850
Yeah.

00:42:29.850 --> 00:42:32.033
I was going to ask for the art side
if you have any like

00:42:32.033 --> 00:42:33.566
of your favorite pieces.

00:42:33.566 --> 00:42:38.216
I've been doing pretty much
most of the unique item art since.

00:42:38.300 --> 00:42:43.083
I guess whenever betrayal happened,
I came, I came on board a little after.
2017?

00:42:45.316 --> 00:42:48.316
maybe? 
The last five years or something like that.

00:42:48.316 --> 00:42:51.350
And so I've done
a lot of the art for them

00:42:51.350 --> 00:42:54.350
and the art has a very different name
to the final game.

00:42:54.350 --> 00:42:55.883
It's not even close.

00:42:55.883 --> 00:42:57.900
An interesting

00:42:57.900 --> 00:43:00.900
one to me is The Shield
everyone knows as the Squire.

00:43:01.050 --> 00:43:04.033
I think it's the thing
with three white sockets. Yep.

00:43:04.033 --> 00:43:06.516
Yeah, I made them have three white
sockets from an art perspective

00:43:06.516 --> 00:43:10.400
Yeah, I remember!
 Because I modeled three white sockets, eye ball things

00:43:10.400 --> 00:43:12.650
things on it and I was like, it's
going to have three white sockets.

00:43:12.650 --> 00:43:14.183
Yeah, I actually remember this.

00:43:14.183 --> 00:43:17.966
And they were like, okay, well,
it was busted anyway.

00:43:18.200 --> 00:43:20.250
So adding the three white sockets to,

00:43:20.250 --> 00:43:21.700
I don't know if it really changed
too much.

00:43:21.700 --> 00:43:23.216
So I just made it more OP

00:43:23.216 --> 00:43:25.666
But on the same day I made that,

00:43:25.666 --> 00:43:28.666
I just made it and they were like,
Oh, we need another shield.

00:43:28.800 --> 00:43:32.516
And I was like, okay,
I'll make a cooler one! So I made a cooler shield

00:43:32.600 --> 00:43:33.683
Visually.

00:43:33.683 --> 00:43:38.066
And that
ended up being the oppressor.

00:43:38.150 --> 00:43:39.233
And I was very bummed.

00:43:39.233 --> 00:43:42.266
Trash the trash!
Definitely wasn't the coolest shield in game

00:43:42.300 --> 00:43:46.316
If knew I would have not made it
that cool looking

00:43:46.400 --> 00:43:49.733
I would’ve dug some trash
out of the unused folder.

00:43:49.800 --> 00:43:53.016
Yeah.

00:43:53.100 --> 00:43:58.383
Let's see what else we've got here

00:43:58.466 --> 00:43:58.850
in terms

00:43:58.850 --> 00:44:02.150
of making art
and I guess items for an act.

00:44:02.150 --> 00:44:06.166
How are you like, getting inspired
or taking inspiration from?

00:44:06.383 --> 00:44:09.816
We have really strong art direction
people.

00:44:09.900 --> 00:44:12.233
Some have come and gone,

00:44:12.233 --> 00:44:14.750
shout out Chander.

00:44:14.750 --> 00:44:15.500
Yeah.

00:44:15.500 --> 00:44:16.200
And they,

00:44:16.200 --> 00:44:20.250
they really just put a really dense
fabric of, of, of thinking over

00:44:20.250 --> 00:44:21.266
all of the acts

00:44:21.266 --> 00:44:25.050
like really going into Maraketh,
Vaal and Karui and others.

00:44:25.050 --> 00:44:27.466
I'm not going to talk about.

00:44:27.466 --> 00:44:31.100
And just, basically we would work
with them and establish like

00:44:31.100 --> 00:44:34.566
common shape language
and like themes and stuff 

00:44:34.650 --> 00:44:39.850
just to make things
feel cohesive and part of that world,

00:44:39.916 --> 00:44:44.283
same kind of patterns
and shapes and stuff like that.

00:44:44.366 --> 00:44:45.716
yeah,

00:44:45.716 --> 00:44:48.716
it's the most interesting part,
I think because it sort of

00:44:48.866 --> 00:44:49.583
you create stuff

00:44:49.583 --> 00:44:53.466
no one's ever seen before kind of
because it's like it just doesn't,

00:44:53.550 --> 00:44:57.400
you know, there's like weapons
made of like cactus wood,

00:44:57.483 --> 00:45:01.083
Like, no one
makes weapons of cactus wood.

00:45:01.166 --> 00:45:01.800
But they were like, oh,

00:45:01.800 --> 00:45:04.800
these people, they
they only have access to cactus wood.

00:45:04.800 --> 00:45:07.800
So the handle has to be cactus
somewhere, right?

00:45:07.950 --> 00:45:11.333
Like I can't have just wood,
otherwise it breaks the theme.

00:45:11.333 --> 00:45:14.333
It's like well hey,
where’d they get that wood from?

00:45:14.566 --> 00:45:15.850
It's like small stuff like that.

00:45:15.850 --> 00:45:18.050
Another question we have here.

00:45:18.050 --> 00:45:18.466
Are there

00:45:18.466 --> 00:45:22.616
