No it won't because

00:45:57.033 --> 00:45:59.566
there will not be any scouring orbs

00:45:59.566 --> 00:46:02.450
Yep! They’re gone!

00:46:02.450 --> 00:46:04.050
If you want another item
You’re going to have to alch

00:46:04.050 --> 00:46:08.166
a white one.

00:46:08.250 --> 00:46:08.783
Why is there

00:46:08.783 --> 00:46:12.616
no 75% Int 25% strength or dex weapon.

00:46:12.633 --> 00:46:17.816
So like why aren't you fitting
more of the pie into the ratio?

00:46:17.900 --> 00:46:20.816
You haven't seen all the weapons yet.

00:46:20.816 --> 00:46:24.166
Maybe..
There actually is a few, but it

00:46:24.266 --> 00:46:25.650
it wouldn't have really, you know,

00:46:25.650 --> 00:46:29.300
looked really nice in that graphic
because some of the staves

00:46:29.300 --> 00:46:32.300
will have skills that are more,

00:46:32.300 --> 00:46:36.366
you know, strength int aligned spell
and then that would actually take up

00:46:36.366 --> 00:46:40.983
the 75% Int 25%
strength section of the tree

00:46:41.066 --> 00:46:44.283
that is slightly more,
you know, nebulous

00:46:44.366 --> 00:46:45.050
like in a little way

00:46:45.050 --> 00:46:48.750
because the caster weapons
don't actually have those base stats

00:46:48.833 --> 00:46:52.166
to, you know, change
as a result of their attributes.

00:46:52.366 --> 00:46:56.550
But it's more just, I suppose,
what attribute requirements,

00:46:56.550 --> 00:47:00.933
the skills that are aligned to that
particular class requires.

00:47:01.016 --> 00:47:02.600
But again, this is Path of Exile

00:47:02.600 --> 00:47:05.916
You're going to use an Int weapon
a strength skill and

00:47:06.083 --> 00:47:10.716
and everything. You know?

00:47:10.800 --> 00:47:13.283
there's just a lot of questions.

00:47:13.283 --> 00:47:18.700
It's really hard to filter
through all of them

00:47:19.100 --> 00:47:23.950
Like there are way
more than I expected.

00:47:24.016 --> 00:47:24.900
Oh, this is a good one.

00:47:24.900 --> 00:47:29.416
How does the art for items
come from the story or the lore

00:47:29.416 --> 00:47:32.666
Does the art
sometimes influence the lore?

00:47:32.750 --> 00:47:35.400
oh... I think that

00:47:35.400 --> 00:47:38.800
sometimes it kind of makes itself up
as it goes.

00:47:38.866 --> 00:47:43.216
But there is- There are times where

00:47:43.300 --> 00:47:46.300
there's obviously characters and they have stuff.

00:47:46.300 --> 00:47:48.916
like there will be bosses
and things that a unique.

00:47:48.916 --> 00:47:50.216
Weapon is just straight up,

00:47:50.216 --> 00:47:53.116
like you get it off them
kind of thing.

00:47:53.116 --> 00:47:54.383
There’s definitely been times

00:47:54.383 --> 00:47:58.300
where we’ve made a unique
with some story behind it

00:47:58.366 --> 00:48:00.950
and then we've expanded on it
at a much later date.

00:48:00.950 --> 00:48:02.516
Yeah,
So it's always nice to have these

00:48:02.516 --> 00:48:07.950
sort of story threads that we can
then follow up on later.

00:48:08.033 --> 00:48:09.300
This could be interesting.

00:48:09.300 --> 00:48:12.900
Was there a memorable unique
you tried to design that couldn't

00:48:12.900 --> 00:48:15.016
be implemented
for a technical reason?

00:48:15.016 --> 00:48:15.500
Oh yes.

00:48:15.500 --> 00:48:21.333
Actually there are so many of these,
but I think my favorite example is

00:48:21.416 --> 00:48:24.766
so there's that helmet
that drops from Kurgal

00:48:24.766 --> 00:48:28.050
The boss in Delve, the Lich from Delve
called Hale Negator

00:48:28.050 --> 00:48:32.200
I think? So
originally the effect of what

00:48:32.266 --> 00:48:35.250
what that helmet was supposed to do
was it was supposed to do what

00:48:35.250 --> 00:48:37.350
the Agnostic Keystone does,

00:48:37.350 --> 00:48:40.166
where it was supposed to drain
your mana and heal your health.

00:48:40.166 --> 00:48:44.333
But for technical reasons
that I don't actually remember now,

00:48:44.550 --> 00:48:48.966
it could not exist on an item
that also had energy shield on it,

00:48:49.050 --> 00:48:53.216
and it couldn't exist unless
it turned off your energy shield.

00:48:53.300 --> 00:48:55.883
So when
we were doing the Legion Keystone-

00:48:55.883 --> 00:48:59.216
so we had to come up with something
completely different in the last week

00:48:59.216 --> 00:49:02.550
before the release-
the release of Delve.

00:49:02.633 --> 00:49:05.116
But I always really love that idea
because it was just

00:49:05.116 --> 00:49:07.916
a really cool thing that, you know,

00:49:07.916 --> 00:49:09.300
And then when we were designing

00:49:09.300 --> 00:49:13.416
those millions of keystones,
when we were doing the Legion,

00:49:13.500 --> 00:49:15.083
you know, like the Timeless Jewels,

00:49:15.083 --> 00:49:17.600
this idea just came back
and I just kept pushing it.

00:49:17.600 --> 00:49:19.400
I was like, you know,
we got to find a way to do this

00:49:19.400 --> 00:49:20.550
because it'll be really awesome.

00:49:20.550 --> 00:49:21.833
And eventually

00:49:21.833 --> 00:49:23.550
the way we were able to do it
was, Well,

00:49:23.550 --> 00:49:25.916
if you turn off Energy Shield entirely,
then we can do it.

00:49:25.916 --> 00:49:28.850
So it sort of works as a downside,
which I mean, it

00:49:28.850 --> 00:49:32.033
probably did need one,
at least at the time, but it also

00:49:32.033 --> 00:49:35.800
was a technical reason
why it needed to exist.

